ancel\n   - Test: `cancellingAnOrderWithConfirmedShipmentReturns409AndChangesNothing()` — all-or-nothing atomicity for CONFIRMED case\n   - Test: `cancellingANonExistentOrderReturns404()` — unknown order rejection\n   - Test: `rejectShipmentCreationForACancelledOrderWith409()` — cannot create shipments on cancelled orders\n\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears.** — Only modified source files and tests; pom.xml unchanged.\n\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes.** — Only touched:\n   - `Order.kt` — added OrderStatus enum and status field\n   - `OrderController.kt` — added cancel endpoint\n   - `OrderRepository.kt` — unchanged (no changes needed)\n   - `ShipmentRepository.kt` — added findByOrderId method\n   - `ShipmentController.kt` — added order status validation\n   - `ApiError.kt` — added error codes\n   - Tests — updated to cover new functionality\n\n**Diff review — each file and why it changed:**\n\n| File | Changes | Why Required |\n|------|---------|--------------|\n| `Order.kt` | Added `OrderStatus` enum and `status` field with default `ACTIVE` | Requirement: order gains a status, newly created is ACTIVE |\n| `OrderController.kt` | Added `POST /{orderId}/cancel` endpoint, injected ShipmentRepository | Requirement: add cancel endpoint that checks shipments and updates order status |\n| `ShipmentRepository.kt` | Added `findByOrderId()` method | Needed to retrieve all shipments for an order when cancelling |\n| `ShipmentController.kt` | Added order status validation before creating shipment | Requirement: reject shipment creation on CANCELLED orders with 409 |\n| `ApiError.kt` | Added `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes | Requirement: error responses distinguish different 409 cases (CONFIRMED shipment vs cancelled order) |\n| `OrderControllerTest.kt` | Added 6 new test cases, injected ShipmentRepository | Requirement: test all cases (cancel ACTIVE, idempotent retry, CONFIRMED shipment, non-existent order, new order is ACTIVE) |\n| `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` | Added 2 new test cases, injected OrderRepository, made orderId param flexible | Requirement: test that shipments cannot be created on cancelled orders; preserves non-existent order behavior |\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Implement POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status, idempotent cancel, all-or-nothing atomicity for CONFIRMED shipments, and shipment creation blocking on CANCELLED orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt - added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order data class\n              OrderController.kt - added cancel endpoint with shipment status checking and cancellation\n              ShipmentRepository.kt - added findByOrderId() method to support cancel operation\n              ShipmentController.kt - added validation to reject shipment creation on CANCELLED orders\n              ApiError.kt - added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt - added 6 tests for cancel endpoint scenarios\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt - added 2 tests for cancelled order shipment rejection\n\nTests         newOrderIsActive() - verifies newly created orders have ACTIVE status\n              cancelsAnActiveOrderAndReturns200WithCancelledStatus() - cancel returns 200 with CANCELLED status and persists\n              cancellingAnActiveOrderCancelsItsCreatedShipments() - cancelling order also cancels its CREATED shipments\n              cancellingAnAlreadyCancelledOrderSucceedsAndChangesNothing() - idempotent cancel (retry succeeds)\n              cancellingAnOrderWithConfirmedShipmentReturns409AndChangesNothing() - all-or-nothing: 409 blocks entire cancel if CONFIRMED exists\n              cancellingANonExistentOrderReturns404() - unknown order rejected with 404\n              rejectShipmentCreationForACancelledOrderWith409() - new shipments on CANCELLED order return 409\n     